+  "title": "GOV-0116: WP-UAT-B — type the uat evidence binding and validate it in the canonical gate (badf-uat DESIGNED → IMPLEMENTED)",
+  "problem": "🧠 **ARCHI (BARCHI-3)** — plan for **WP-UAT-B**: `badf-uat` `DESIGNED` → `IMPLEMENTED`. `WP-2026-0124` / `BADF-DEM-0110`.\n\n## Stage-Gate\n\n- **Stage:** 10 (UAT), rung B of the A→E ladder frozen in `skills/badf-uat/references/acceptance.md` at WP-UAT-A (#241, landed `c525129`).\n- **Decision:** Continue. Rung A froze the contract and shipped **no runtime**; `uat` is a required G10 evidence type that no gate path can mechanically check.\n- **Over-engineering risk refused:** registering execution adapters (`browser-uat`, `api-uat`), building a scenario-derivation engine, or adding a second gate. B types the artifacts and extends the canonical gate. Nothing executes a scenario at this rung.\n- **Lean mode:** advisory.\n\n## What rung A committed B to, verbatim\n\n> `IMPLEMENTED` — **WP-UAT-B**: typed `uat` evidence schema specializing `evidence.schema.json`; the UAT Scenario object, the execution-observation record and the two-layer disposition record as typed artifacts; a `badf_gate.py` path validating a G10 `uat` dossier's typed objects — mirroring `verify` for G08. Extends the canonical gate; adds no second one.\n\nThis plan implements exactly that and nothing beyond it.\n\n## Precedent being mirrored\n\n`WP-VAL-B` (#247, `badf-release-validation` → IMPLEMENTED) and `WP-VER-B` (G08) established the shape: a typed schema per evidence type specializing `evidence.schema.json` with a `binding` object, plus a `check_gNN_binding` registered in `EVIDENCE_RULES` — **strictly additive**, so untyped objects stay admissible and nothing already landed breaks. `uat` is **one** type rather than four, so this is a smaller surface than VAL-B's.\n\n## Scope\n\n- **`schemas/uat.schema.json`** — typed `binding` carrying, per the frozen invariants:\n\n  | field | invariant |\n  | --- | --- |\n  | `candidate` | UAT-I04 — the exact immutable candidate accepted |\n  | `acceptance_basis` | UAT-I05 — exact PRD / acceptance-criteria / RTM digests |\n  | `scenarios[]` | UAT-I01/I02/I06/I07 — source refs, actor, business-readable oracle, criticality |\n  | `observations[]` | UAT-I09 — adapter, observed outcome, result, executed_by |\n  | `defects[]` | UAT-I11 — the ten-way class enum, `ACCEPTANCE_CRITERION_DEFECT` among them |\n  | `coverage` | UAT-I12/I13 — per-criterion state, roles, journeys, declared non-coverage |\n  | `recommendation` | UAT-I14 — `RECOMMEND_*` only |\n  | `acceptance` (optional) | UAT-I15/I16 — Layer 2, binding Layer 1's digests |\n\n- **`check_g10_uat_binding`** in `badf_gate.py`, registered `EVIDENCE_RULES[\"uat\"]`.\n- **`tests/test_badf_uat_evidence.py`** — schema-shape and binding tests.\n\n## The one thing this rung must not get wrong\n\n**The recommendation vocabulary must not be able to express an acceptance.** `RECOMMEND_ACCEPT` / `RECOMMEND_ACCEPT_WITH_CONDITIONS` / `RECOMMEND_REJECT` / `RECOMMEND_INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE` are the closed enum; `ACCEPTED`, `ACCEPTED_WITH_CONDITIONS` and `REJECTED` are valid **only** inside the optional Layer 2 `acceptance` object, which additionally requires a human `accepted_by`. A schema that let `recommendation: \"ACCEPTED\"` validate would let the evidence producer issue the decision it is forbidden from making — UAT-I14 defeated by a permissive enum rather than by an argument.\n\n## Tests (failing-first, each observed red)\n\n- `test_uat_schema_specializes_evidence_and_is_additive` — untyped `uat` evidence still validates.\n- `test_recommendation_enum_cannot_express_an_acceptance` — `recommendation: \"ACCEPTED\"` is **refused**.\n- `test_layer2_acceptance_requires_a_human_principal` — `accepted_by` absent or non-human → refused.\n- `test_layer2_must_bind_layer1_digests` — `acceptance.candidate_digest` ≠ `binding.candidate` → refused.\n- `test_defect_class_is_the_frozen_ten` — an invented class is refused; `ACCEPTANCE_CRITERION_DEFECT` accepted.\n- `test_declared_non_coverage_is_required_not_optional` — UAT-I12.\n- `test_untyped_binding_is_still_admissible` — additivity, the property VAL-B's rung established.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nAny execution adapter or subskill registration · scenario derivation logic · deterministic G10 controls (that is **WP-UAT-C**, lean **disabled** — HARD INVARIANTS) · any `lifecycle.json` change · any second gate (UAT-I20) · `badf-production-readiness`'s two types.\n\n## Ladder position and gating\n\nB is **shared-surface** (`schemas/`, `badf_gate.py`) → **QA + REV**, unlike rung A which was ladder-internal. Queues behind the current landing order; expect rebases.\n\n**Version tier:** minor (new schema + new gate path, backward-compatible). **Ids:** `WP-2026-0124` / `BADF-DEM-0110` / `GOV-0116`, swept clean on all four surfaces — main + remote heads, open-PR file lists, issue/PR titles and bodies, and my own unpushed worktree.\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
